before:
Consider the vector space ${\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\times 2$ matrices over $R.$

Which of the following statements are true?

I. $$
\displaystyle \{\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\ 0 & 0\end{bmatrix},\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\ 0 & 1\end{bmatrix}\}
$$ is a linearly independent set in ${\text{M}}_{2}(R)$

II. $$
\displaystyle \begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\ 0 & 5\end{bmatrix}
$$ can be expressed as a linear combination of $$
\displaystyle \{\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\ 0 & 0\end{bmatrix},\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\ 0 & 1\end{bmatrix}\}
$$

III. $$
\displaystyle \{\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\ 0 & 0\end{bmatrix},\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\ 0 & 1\end{bmatrix}\}
$$ is a basis of ${\text{M}}_{2}(R)$

